================================================================================
1. WHAT THE DISTRIBUTION CONTAINS
================================================================================

DAP is a standalone analytics engine: engine-native/ (Java 21, DuckDB, Arrow,
Javalin) and adapters/mcp/ (a stdio MCP adapter, Python standard library only).
It contains no KNIME code, does not link org.knime and does not ship the KNIME
runtime or catalog.

================================================================================
2. THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS
================================================================================

engine-native/target/dap-native.jar bundles:

  Component                    License                Upstream
  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  DuckDB JDBC 1.5.6.0          MIT                    https://duckdb.org/
  Apache Arrow Java 19.0.0     Apache-2.0             https://arrow.apache.org/
  Javalin 6.7.0                Apache-2.0             https://javalin.io/
  Eclipse Jetty 11.0.25        EPL-2.0 or Apache-2.0  https://jetty.org/
  Jackson 2.19.0 / 2.21.0      Apache-2.0             https://github.com/FasterXML/jackson
  SLF4J 2.0.17                 MIT                    https://www.slf4j.org/
  Logback 1.5.18               EPL-1.0 or LGPL-2.1    https://logback.qos.ch/

Test-only dependencies (not shipped): JUnit 5 (EPL-2.0), Maven Wrapper.

The jar contains one DuckDB native library for the build platform
(osx_universal, linux_amd64, linux_arm64 or windows_amd64); the shade profiles
exclude the others. Cross-platform packaging can include all four on request.

================================================================================
3. DATA FIXTURES
================================================================================

tests/goldens-native/data/ contains small public example datasets (iris, adult,
worldbank countries, air quality) used by the golden suite. They are test data,
not part of the engine.
